course: dictionary
lesson: 8182
title: Respectfully
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Respectfully is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It means in a polite way that shows you value someone and their feelings. When you listen respectfully, you pay attention and do not interrupt.
explain: «When responding to another team, you begin with what was good in their view, then add to it or question it respectfully.» Here respectfully tells you how to question: politely, not rudely. You can still disagree, but you show care for the other person.
explain: Respectfully also helps when you disagree. «Respectfully, I think you are wrong.» The word softens what follows, so the other person can hear you without feeling put down. Try swapping in rudely and see how the sentence changes.
fact: Respectfully means in a polite way that shows you value someone and their feelings.
fact: «Respectfully» is also used when politely disagreeing: «Respectfully, I think you are wrong.»
fact: Phrases you may see are «listen respectfully», «speak respectfully», «respectfully disagree» and «Yours respectfully».
fact: At memorials, people stand respectfully in silence.
fact: «Some rules are unfair and should be challenged respectfully», which means speaking up calmly, not breaking the rule in secret.
exercise: «A respectful tone means speaking calmly, using names respectfully and thanking the other team.» What does respectfully mean in this sentence? | In a secret way, so nobody hears | *In a polite way that shows you value people | In a hurried way, so the talk ends fast | In a loud and angry way
exercise: Asha says, «Respectfully, I think you are wrong.» What is she doing? | Laughing at the other person | Agreeing completely | *Politely disagreeing | Walking away without a word
exercise: Some rules are unfair. What does it mean to challenge such a rule respectfully? | Break the rule where nobody can see | Pretend the rule does not exist | *Speak up calmly and politely about it | Shout at the teacher until they give in
test: Which phrase is a polite way to end a letter? | Yours secretly | Yours rudely | *Yours respectfully | Yours loudly
test: Which is the best way to listen respectfully to a classmate? | Laugh before they have finished | Talk over them while they speak | Look at your phone | *Look at them, wait for them to finish, and do not interrupt
exam: What is the opposite of respectfully? | Gently | Kindly | Politely | *Rudely
